      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Jiabin!\n\nWhat we do in StreamOutHalLocal:\n\n  std::basic_string\u003cuint8_t\u003e((uint8_t*)param)\n\ndoes make sense to me as it invokes the overload of the constructor which takes the \u0027param\u0027 data in and then \u0027Constructs the string with the contents initialized with a copy of the null-terminated character string pointed to by s. The length of the string is determined by the first null character.\u0027\n\nBut doing what the CL is proposing:\n\n  std::basic_string\u003cuint8_t\u003e metadataBs \u003d\n     *reinterpret_cast\u003cstd::basic_string\u003cuint8_t\u003e *\u003e(param);\n\nis different--it is reinterpeting \u0027param\u0027 as a string object, which seems incorrect to me.",
